          <p>
            Budget for filters and bags. A fine dust or HEPA cartridge can cost $25 to $60, and bags run a few dollars each. A cyclone separator costs $30 to $100 plus a bucket. These are worth the money: they extend motor and filter life and make the vac far more effective on fine dust.
          </p>

          <p>
            For most homeowners, a 12 to 14-gallon vac with a 2-1/2-inch hose, a drain port and good filter options is the best balance of capability and cost. Add a compact vac or a cordless one if you need portability, and step up to an extractor only if you sand indoors often. If you are also planning a planer for the shop, check the dust collection guidance in our <a href="/best-benchtop-planer/">benchtop planer guide</a> before choosing.
          </p>
