          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most garages and home workshops, the Ridgid HD1400 NXT is the vac to buy: a 2-1/2-inch hose, a drain port, a sensible 14-gallon tank and filters you can find anywhere. Pick the Craftsman 16-gallon for frequent water and renovation work, the Vacmaster Beast if you also want a shop blower, and a compact DeWalt or Shop-Vac for cars and small messes. Woodworkers who sand indoors should look seriously at a dust extractor like the Fein Turbo II.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, choose by hose diameter and airflow rather than peak horsepower, match the filter to the dust, and add a bag or cyclone separator for fine material. Pull the paper filter before wet pickup, keep flammables and hot ash out of the tank, and clean the filter often.
